            "review_title": "Review at Ancient VietNam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "pink00flamingo\nLondon, United Kingdom210 contributions\n0\nExcellent food and service\nJan 2019 • Friends\nBeing vegetarian I was struggling to find a good place to eat as the majority of restaurants are serving only seafood, which is the area's speciality. This place looked clean and the staff were very friendly and the menu had a lot of veggie options. Not everyone spoke English but that's fine as the menu is very descriptive and we were all smiling and laughing at our bad pronunciations. I got the sense that a lot locals eat here or pop in to see the staff which gave it a nice neighbourhoodly feel rather than just another tourist restaurant.\n\nI had fresh peach iced tea and a fruit smoothie. Both excellent. The tofu 'starter' was huge and more like a main meal but matched with the dipping sauce was very good. I had veggie rice and deep fried veggie spring rolls. All good and the left-overs were packaged up for me to take away. I still have the lovely carved chop-sticks they gave me.\n\nYou can sit inside or outside next to the little koi river/pond. I really like this place and would have eaten here again if I'd had the time.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 14, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
