            "review_title": "Review at Ancient VietNam Restaurant",
            "review_text": "ruthandvern\nWilton, California15640 contributions\n0\nWhat a glorious glimpse of an storied history\nApr 2018 • Couples\nThe two story eatery with outdoor seating and casual swings brings you a warm feeling of going home to eat with family and friends. It has plenty of room for these gatherings. Plenty of windows on a wide street with parking. There are ample wait staff, we were seated quickly. The menu is extensive. What a wide variety of meals incorporating all the local proteins. Vern ordered the ginger pork, a good size serving of boneless pork slices in a very tasty sauce. We shared one clay pot of baked rice (that would make me happy all by itself). I ordered the stir fried tiger prawns with roasted garlic. Outstanding! My wonderful Vern cleaned them, seven chubby succulent prawns that were already prepared for quick removal of the head, shell and tails. We enjoyed our meal immensely.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 27, 2018",
